BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (      The spring held a wondrous power: any silver dropped into its waters would transform into ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (        three times its worth in gold. But only the Keeper could retrieve the gold and decide ho) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (        w to divide it.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (      The first day, the Giver approached with doubt, offering only one coin. It became three go) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (        lden coins, and the Keeper, seeing the Giver's caution, returned one. Both walked away w) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (        ith little gain.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (      The second day, the Giver remembered: *trust multiplies blessings*. He offered three coins) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (        . They became nine golden coins. The Keeper, recognizing the Giver's faith, returned fiv) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (        e. Both prospered.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (      On the third day, the Giver brought all five coins. They transformed into fifteen golden c) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (        oins. The Keeper, honored by such trust, returned eight. Both grew wealthy beyond measur) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (        e.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (      The wanderers learned: when the Giver trusts generously and the Keeper honors that trust f) Tj ET
