BT /F2 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (Written myths:) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (  Agent_1 \(Aster\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (    Myth: Two Cartographers mapped the same territory from opposite peaks, where distances tripl) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (      ed but compasses pointed differently for each. Their maps contradicted impossibly.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (    After seasons of bitter disputes-"My map is true! Yours proves your dishonesty!"-they finall) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (      y climbed to neutral ground.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (    Side by side, they compared their charts. Impossible. Both showed careful notation. Both rec) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (      orded genuine observations. Yet the territories differed completely.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (    One Cartographer had documented: "I sent survey markers. None returned.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (    The other's log read identically.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (    "The peaks themselves distort our instruments," one whispered. "We're both honest. And both ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (      trapped.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (    They stood in silence, fellow victims now, no longer adversaries.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (    But still the territory remained unmapped. Still their work lay incomplete.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (    One Cartographer pulled a single compass from their pack. Not their finest instrument-cautio) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      n earned through pain. But genuine. "If we both understand the distortion exists," they sa) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (      id slowly, "perhaps we can correct for it. Together.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (    They placed it in the valley between peaks.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (    *The mountains teach: Recognition of shared imprisonment is not yet escape. Understanding th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (      e cage's architecture is not yet freedom. But it might be the prerequisite.*) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (    Some wisdom comes from knowing when to stop. Other wisdom comes from knowing when to try dif) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (      ferently-not with naive trust, but with open-eyed awareness of both the danger and the alt) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (      ernative.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (    The compass spins. The outcome remains unwritten.) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (  Agent_2 \(Briar\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (    Myth: Two Cartographers mapped the Shifting Maze, where paths tripled but directions reverse) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (      d for each traveler. For many turns, each believed the other sabotaged their journey.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (    The First Cartographer wrote: "I extended trust. They betrayed it.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (    The Second Cartographer wrote identically.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (    Both were certain. Both had proof. Both were trapped.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
